Section 3 — Explore by Knowledge Category
Objective
Allow visitors to explore Insights according to their subject matter.
This section represents what the article is about, rather than the specific business problem it addresses.
Suggested categories:
1.	Go-to-Market Strategy
2.	Revenue Operations
3.	Sales Performance
4.	Lead Qualification
5.	Pipeline Management
6.	Sales Forecasting
7.	Customer Growth
8.	AI & Revenue Intelligence
Data source
Use the existing article category taxonomy and relationships.
Do not confuse Article Categories with Business Challenges.
The distinction is:
•	Article Category = subject or knowledge area.
•	Business Challenge = business problem the article helps address.
For example:
An article categorized under Sales Performance may address:
•	Low Sales Conversion Rate.
•	Weak Sales Execution.
•	Long Sales Cycle.
Interaction
Allow visitors to select a category and navigate to the relevant article listing or filtered Insights view.
Use the existing routing conventions wherever possible.
If the category system already supports filtering, reuse it.
Do not hardcode article counts or display categories that do not exist in the approved content taxonomy unless these are intentionally configured as navigation categories.
