5. Business Challenge Data Retrieval and Performance
This is a critical technical requirement.
The dynamic Business Challenge section must be efficient and compatible with the existing RevOS SSG architecture.
5.1 Avoid inefficient database queries
Do not create a separate Supabase request for every Business Challenge if the entire section can be retrieved through a more efficient query.
Prefer an optimized query or database function that retrieves:
•	Active Business Challenges.
•	Their published Insight articles.
•	Relevant article metadata.
•	Primary challenge relationship.
Avoid N+1 query patterns.
If necessary, implement a dedicated Supabase RPC function or reusable data-access function, but only if the existing architecture does not already provide a suitable solution.
Do not expose sensitive database data.
Use the appropriate public read permissions and existing RLS policies.
5.2 Static Site Generation compatibility
The public Insights page is intended to use the existing SSG architecture.
Therefore:
•	Retrieve published content during the SSG build process.
•	Generate the initial HTML for the Insights page with the Business Challenge groups and article information included.
•	Ensure that search engines can read the challenge names, descriptions, and article links in the generated HTML.
•	Avoid rendering an empty section that only becomes populated after browser-side JavaScript executes.
•	Reuse the existing React rendering and hydration architecture.
•	Ensure server-rendered HTML and client hydration use compatible initial data.
Do not introduce a separate SSR server.
Do not move HTML generation into a Supabase Edge Function.
Wasmer remains the static hosting platform.
5.3 Content publishing integration
The existing content publishing automation should trigger the SSG rebuild when relevant published content changes.
Ensure that the existing publishing workflow accounts for:
•	Publishing a new Insight article.
•	Updating a published Insight article.
•	Unpublishing an Insight article.
•	Deleting a published article.
•	Changing a published article's Business Challenge associations.
•	Changing a Business Challenge name, description, status, or display order.
If an existing publishing event mechanism already supports these changes, extend it rather than creating a second publishing workflow.
The result should be that the Insights page reflects the latest eligible content after a successful build and deployment.
