10. Loading, Empty, and Error States
Implement appropriate states.
Loading
If client-side loading is used for any non-SSG supplementary functionality, show a lightweight loading state.
The main Business Challenge groups should already be present in the SSG-generated HTML.
Empty states
If there are no active Business Challenges with published Insight articles:
•	Do not display empty challenge groups.
•	Either hide Section 4 or display a deliberate fallback message with a link to Latest Insights.
•	Do not display placeholder or fabricated challenge data.
If there are no published Insights:
•	Display a professional empty state.
•	Do not render broken or empty article cards.
Error states
If the SSG content retrieval fails:
•	Fail the build or use an explicitly approved fallback strategy.
•	Do not silently deploy a page that appears complete but has lost all dynamic challenge content.
•	Log the error with sufficient diagnostic information.
For optional sections such as Recommended Insights, a clearly defined fallback may be acceptable.
Do not allow a temporary data retrieval problem to overwrite a previously valid production site with incomplete content.
